@startuml
title E05 - Persistence, recovery and bounded storage
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
control "N05\nNode storage" as N05
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
control "B03\nEvent ingestion" as B03
control "B04\nIncident workflow" as B04
control "B05\nNotification routing" as B05
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
actor "Operations engineer" as Ops
N05 -> N05: Append business event before transmit; set gap marker on full
N05 -> H02: Replay retained event after reboot/link recovery
H02 -> H02: Commit once with CRC/marker target implementation
H02 -> H08: Expose unacknowledged cloud outbox
H08 -> B03: Replay with stable event ID and original time
B03 -> B04: Create/reuse incident effect by stable key
B04 -> B05: Create/reuse unique route jobs
B03 -> B08: Append audit/diagnostic record
Ops -> B08: Run backup/restore and retention diagnostics
B08 --> Ops: Return counts, gaps, backlog and restore evidence
note over N05,Ops: Bounded storage must signal loss; no layer silently drops business evidence.
note over N05,Ops: Outcome - Stable identities and layered journals support reboot/outage recovery while surfacing overflow or restore failures.
@enduml
